# Licensing

Copyright (c) 2026 Asger Alstrup Palm and the pure-Weyl gravity programme
contributors.

This repository contains two kinds of material and licenses them separately.
The split is by *kind of file*, not by directory, because most directories
here mix executable verifiers with the certificates and prose they produce.

## Software — MIT

The following are licensed under the MIT License, reproduced in full in
`LICENSE-MIT.txt`:

- Python sources (`*.py`)
- Lean sources (`*.lean`)
- Shell scripts (`*.sh`)
- Wolfram Language sources (`*.wl`)
- build, CI, and configuration files (`ci/`, `*.toml`, `.gitignore`)

## Manuscripts, data, and documentation — CC BY 4.0

Everything else is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International License (CC BY 4.0), reproduced in full in
`LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0.txt` and summarized at
<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>. This includes:

- LaTeX manuscripts and their compiled PDFs (`paper/`)
- notes, reports, and planning documents (`notes/`, `reports/`, `planning/`,
  `*.md`)
- machine-readable certificates, claim maps, evidence-graph data, and
  verification receipts (`*.json`, `*.tsv`, `*.forge`, `*.sha256`, `*.dot`)
- figures and diagrams (`*.svg`, `*.png`)

Attribution should cite the programme and the specific manuscript or
certificate relied upon, together with the commit hash or release tag of the
version used.

## Scope and disclaimers

These licenses grant permission to use, copy, modify, and redistribute the
material. They do not constitute a warranty of scientific correctness, and
they are independent of the claim-lifecycle and dependency-tag boundaries
recorded in the manuscripts and certificates. A permissive license on a file
is not an endorsement of any claim that file makes.

The DTU Compute affiliation recorded in the manuscripts describes an academic
role and does not imply institutional endorsement or licensing authority.

Third-party material quoted or reproduced under fair use / fair dealing —
including published results, equations, and coefficients attributed to their
original authors in the bibliographies — remains under its original terms and
is not relicensed here.
